Subject: terrain from buffer objects, one quadtree walk (ETR_GL_TERRAIN)

The original walks the quadtree once for each terrain type, draws from client arrays (Mesa copies every vertex from the lowest to the highest index of the draw, ~200 KB for 130 triangles, 13 times a frame) and writes the alpha of each vertex into the array before each draw.

Now one walk puts the triangles in lists by terrain, in the order the walks had; positions and normals are a buffer object made once per course; the alpha of a vertex in a pass (terrain >= pass, terrain == pass) is a buffer of 4 bytes a vertex, made when a pass first needs it. Blended passes that add nothing (a terrain no vertex of the three-terrain triangles has) are not drawn.

